  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-06-16T00:29:17.918Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As a desktop user, i often play as 3rd person in other games, vrchat does not offer this at all. There are tweaks that are available to get around this like adding a camera on under the the skins hierarchy but ill end up struggling seeing the menu from a certain distance. A benefit is that people can check their skin for mistakes or issues as they can rotate, zoom around their skin rather than relying on mirrors that don't properly display things accurately. This option also offers a better view with seeing your surroundings as well. The Fov setting should also be an option, as it gives a wider view range on first and 3rd person perspectives, this feature would also reduce the UI canvas size for big monitors as its currently too big for the size. i truly hope the developers would consider implementing this.",
